From: RCTools GPU audit
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/kgsl: harden Channel old-kernel and headless paths

Base: lfdevs/mesa-for-android-container
Commit: 98f3d6229d61452cef80f8563af7c56ae599dc14

Changes:
* skip generic DRM PCI probing when the explicit loader override is kgsl;
* require an actual DRI3 X extension before the KGSL DRI3 fd shortcut;
* support legacy handle-based Android ION after the new fd-returning ALLOC
  ioctl is rejected with ENOTTY/EINVAL;
* avoid NULL dereferences and release KGSL allocation IDs if
  fd_bo_from_handle() fails.

The legacy ION transaction sequence was validated on the real Channel kernel
with the temporary libion-legacy preload shim.  This source patch still
requires full real-device regression testing before replacing the known-good
Mesa runtime.

